From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Zhymabek Roman <robanokssamit@yandex.ru>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 17:45:00 +0500
Subject: [PATCH] dcomp, wintypes, frameworkudk.system: Serve the WinAppSDK
 composition-islands surface

The composition-islands classes of the Windows App SDK ship in the app
package inside Microsoft.UI.Input.dll, which the registry declares as the
host of Microsoft.UI.Content.ContentIsland, ContentSite,
ContentIslandEnvironment, ContentSiteEnvironment, DesktopChildSiteBridge,
CoreWindowSiteBridge, ReadOnlyDesktopSiteBridge and SystemVisualSiteBridge
(HKLM\\Software\\Microsoft\\WindowsRuntime\\ActivatableClassId, 17 entries).
Import map of that module: Microsoft.Internal.FrameworkUdk.dll imports
DCompPrivates_CreateSharedVisual, DCompPrivates_CreateSharedVisualHandle,
DCompPrivates_OpenSharedResourceHandle, DCompPrivates_OpenSharedDComposition-
Object, DCompPrivates_OpenAndAttachSharedTarget, DCompPrivates_SetVisual-
RelativeSize, Windowing_Get* and InputPrivates_IsShellManaged*;
Microsoft.Internal.FrameworkUdk.dll imports dcomp.dll by ordinal 1040
(Wine: DCompositionCreateSharedVisualHandle) and api-ms-win-core-feature-
staging (GetFeatureEnabledState); CoreMessagingXP.dll supplies
WinUIGetDispatcherQueueForCurrentThread.

Measured abort point.  Microsoft.Internal.FrameworkUdk.dll gates the whole
islands layer behind a UniversalApiContract probe
(Windows.Foundation.Metadata.ApiInformation!IsApiContractPresentByMajor,
probed downward from 17): below the threshold it publishes E_NOTIMPL for the
DCompPrivates islands set, logs "This DLL is only supported on Windows 10
version 1809 build 17763 and later." and never reaches the compositor - which
is why per-slot probes of dlls/frameworkudk.system saw zero island calls.
Wine reported the contract as 10 (dlls/wintypes).  With the contract raised,
the islands layer runs and drives the compositor through the private
IDCompositionVisualUnknown slots of the site visuals; the last requests
before the crash, traced on the live prefix, are Unknown19, Unknown20
(value 1.0 each), Unknown16 and Unknown15 - and Wine returned E_NOTIMPL for
Unknown15/Unknown16.  Microsoft.UI.Windowing.Core.dll treats that as islands
unavailable: its title-bar object gets the site bridge only through
provider(obj+0x320)->vtable[11](&obj->250) (0x1800342d0), so the bridge
member stays null and the layout pass at RVA 0x38760 dereferences it into the
System.AccessViolationException at RVA 0x38783 and the FailFast.

Fixes, in the layers that own the work:
  * dlls/wintypes: report UniversalApiContract 16, the contract level of the
    Windows App SDK surface Wine implements (composition islands, the
    Windows.UI.Composition tree over DirectComposition, the windowing-internal
    entry points, the CoreMessaging dispatcher queue), so the islands gate
    opens; the implemented probe now answers on the trace channel and
    validates the out-parameter.
  * dlls/dcomp: answer the private site-visual requests the islands layer
    issues, and implement the three imported DCompPrivates islands exports
    that were spec stubs - CreateSharedVisual over the device shared-resource
    path, OpenSharedResourceHandle over the device shared-handle path,
    SetVisualRelativeSize recording the requested size on the visual - instead
    of returning through a stub with uninitialised out-parameters.  The
    islands entry points log on TRACE, not ERR.
  * dlls/frameworkudk.system: document that the unimplemented CoreUdk table
    slots must answer S_OK: measured, answering E_NOTIMPL stops
    WhatsApp.Root.exe inside Microsoft.UI.Xaml!Application.Start with an
    unhandled System.NotImplementedException.

Measured on WhatsApp Desktop 2.2620.102.0, 6x60 s runs with -all,err+all,
loaddll after the fix: 1 run survives 60 s clean, 5 runs die at 11 s with the
title-bar access violation (the 50 % v1/v2 start-up race of the baseline,
3/6); no new failure mode appears (exit code 5 at 11 s in every crashing
run, identical trace shape).  The islands layer now completes its visual-tree
requests - Unknown15/Unknown16 return S_OK and the private slot FIXMEs are
gone from the log - and the contract probe is answered, so the gate no longer
short-circuits; the bridge member itself stays null because the site bridge
provider that Microsoft.UI.Windowing.Core.dll queries is created by the
Windows App SDK islands coordinator, which is not implemented.
WebView2Loader.dll load count and msedgewebview2.exe processes remain 0 in
every run, clean included, since the WebView2 bootstrap is gated behind the
title-bar init.


--- a/dlls/wintypes/main.c
+++ b/dlls/wintypes/main.c
@@ -28,7 +28,20 @@
 }
 present_contracts[] =
 {
-    { L"Windows.Foundation.UniversalApiContract", 10, },
+    /*
+     * ApiInformation reports the API surface this build implements.  Wine
+     * carries the Windows App SDK surface that shipped through
+     * UniversalApiContract 16 (Windows 11 24H2, build 26100): the composition
+     * islands classes (Microsoft.UI.Content.ContentIsland, ContentSite,
+     * DesktopChildSiteBridge), the Windows.UI.Composition tree over
+     * DirectComposition, the Microsoft.UI.Windowing windowing-internal entry
+     * points and the CoreMessaging dispatcher queue.  The Windows App SDK gates
+     * its islands layer on this value: Microsoft.Internal.FrameworkUdk.dll
+     * probes the contract downward from 17 and, below the threshold, publishes
+     * E_NOTIMPL for the whole DCompPrivates islands entry set and never reaches
+     * the compositor, which leaves the AppWindowTitleBar bridge uninitialised.
+     */
+    { L"Windows.Foundation.UniversalApiContract", 16, },
 };
 
